{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1774298746,"nonce":"SZSXcxffGDpcYnckDiJyOAuJIWo=","title":"Auth hooks: missing rebuild SSE broadcast and daemon restart after merge","message":"When the auth_hooks system (Bug: 4afab83) replaced the old auth-merge.sh build/restart logic, only the build step was preserved. The restart and SSE notification were dropped.\n\nCurrent behavior after a Mandible self-merge:\n1. auth-merge.sh completes the merge\n2. auth_hooks executor runs \"npm install \u0026\u0026 npm run build\" (builtin hook)\n3. Dist files are updated on disk\n4. Nothing else happens — daemon keeps serving old code from memory, no SSE event, no splash screen\n\nExpected behavior:\n1. Broadcast mandible:rebuilding SSE event before running hooks (triggers splash screen)\n2. After hooks complete, restart the daemon (launchctl kickstart or process.exit with launchd respawn)\n\nThe splash screen mechanism (Bug: 326a3e2) is wired correctly in the UI — it listens for mandible:rebuilding on SSE and shows the splash. The problem is purely that nobody emits the event or restarts the daemon.\n\nFix: In auth-queue.ts executeHooks path (~line 800), for the mandible repo specifically:\n- Broadcast mandible:rebuilding before running hooks\n- After hooks succeed, exit the process (launchd respawns automatically)","files":null}]}